# Backend Technique Enhancement Step 6 / Remaining Work Log

## Status

- Started: 2026-09-21
- Scope: remaining technique enhancements, bass-line patterns, advanced reharmonization, response expansion
- Status: Complete

## Implemented

- Added bass-line pattern output to `ProgressionAnalyzer`:
  - descending bass line
  - ascending bass line
  - pedal point
- Added advanced technique matchers:
  - tritone substitution
  - backdoor dominant
  - chromatic mediant
  - passing diminished
  - common-tone diminished
- Added secondary leading-tone diminished seed and matcher in the previous enhancement step.
- Extended the seed rule set to 13 rules.
- Added technique alternatives to the primary technique result.
- Added analysis request context to the API response.
- Added progression alternatives to the analysis response.
- Preserved existing FE fields `technique.id`, `technique.name`, and `technique.description`.

## Scope Decisions

- Bass-line analysis uses one chord per bar in the current block analyzer. Multi-chord bars remain excluded from block-level progression analysis.
- Advanced diminished and chromatic rules use conservative structural heuristics rather than attempting full voicing-level inference.
- `alternatives`, `progressionAlternatives`, `confidence`, `evidence`, and `context` are additive response fields.

